From c3da5dab613fcfef13c969f1ffdf4649d19ac05f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MeepingsCorner <MeepingsCorner@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:45:47 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Index Rust lifetimes, raw strings, pub(crate) and C export
 attributes

- mask: a ' followed by an identifier not closed by ' is a lifetime or
  label, not a char literal; 'a' and C multi-char 'RIFF' stay literals.
  &'static str used to blank code up to the next ', mismatching braces
  so every later function in the file vanished (70 of 159 in one file).
- mask: Rust raw strings r".." / r#".."# / br##".."## are one literal.
- wide header: accept a lifetime in a return type (-> &'static str).
- headers: skip pub(crate)/pub(super), __declspec(..), __attribute__((..)).
  pub(crate) fn f( was indexed as a function named pub taking crate.
- selftest: four new checks (93/93).

On a 563-file Rust+C tree: +643 real functions, 88 phantom 'pub' and
2 phantom call-site entries removed, no real function lost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016F56dCPHR8NvAW5WGDRyH8
